'''''Marsilea mutica''''', known as the '''large-leaved nardoo''', is a species of aquatic [[fern]] in the family [[Marsileaceae]]. A widespread species with wide [[clover]] like fronds, found in freshwater marshes, mostly in Australia and nearby [[New Caledonia]]. Seen in floating in deeper water than other ferns in the same genus.<ref name="RBGS">{{cite web |last1=Wilson |first1=Peter |title=''Marsilea mutica'' |url=http://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?page=nswfl&lvl=sp&name=Marsilea~mutica |publisher=Royal Botanic Garden Sydney |access-date=1 June 2024}}</ref><ref>Les Robinson - Field Guide to the Native Plants of Sydney, {{ISBN|978-0-7318-1211-0}} page 433</ref>

